Howdy,

   This is a little text file to help you get DeepSpace running on your CNET
BBS.  DeepSpace was originally written as a DOS door and previously tested
on E! BBS only.  Well, I happened into the programmers here in Spokane and
got it to run on my CNET bbs for them and here is how it's done:

1.  In your PFILES: directory, make a directory called DeepSpace.

2.  Uncompress the DeepSpace archive into the Deepspace directory.  Your
    directory tree should now look something like this:

   Pfiles:DeepSpace/Text (dir)
                    DeepSpace
                    DeepHost
                    DeepSet
                    DeepSpace.guide
                    DS_TA.lha
                    sysop.notes
                    Gamesetup

3.  Run the executable GAMESETUP.  Note that you must fill in the PATH or
    the setup will fail.

4.  Somewhere in your USER-STARTUP put the following line:

    run pfiles:Deepspace/deephost <nil: >nil:

5.  Add DeepSpace as a DOS door with the following options:  (Note:  Keep in
    mind that this is the setup per CNET 3.05c.)

DOS filename:  Pfiles:deepspace/deepspace
Description :  DeepSpace
Arguments   :  %1 T=%7 CNET ECHO A=5 ASKRIP

Disable MORE?  YES
Raw Console Startup?  YES

6.  Reboot your computer to start the DeepHost server and you should be good
    to go.

